  "rulesOverviewTitle": "Goal and setup",
  "rulesOverview": "For 4–8 players: one player is the secret Impostor and the others are Innocent. Deal 4 cards and give each player 3 Hearts. Keep roles secret.",
  "rulesTurnTitle": "Your turn",
  "rulesTurn": "Draw 2 cards, take up to 2 actions, and discard down to 7 cards. You may attack at most once per turn. If the draw pile runs out, shuffle the discard pile.",
  "rulesEvidenceTitle": "Suspicion and Evidence",
  "rulesEvidence": "Suspicion is public and ranges from 0 to 3; successful attack damage and Noisy actions increase it. It does not prove a role. Clue and Behavior Evidence belong to an investigator and a specific suspect. Use one action to observe a qualifying past attack or Noisy action for Behavior Evidence. The first Investigation against a player at 3 Suspicion each turn costs no action.",
  "rulesAttackTitle": "Attacks and recovery",
  "rulesAttack": "Attack another Active player. The target may defend; if they pass, others may Step In in order. An unblocked attack costs the target 1 Heart. At 0 Hearts, they are Cornered, not eliminated. If still Cornered at their next scheduled turn, they recover to 1 Heart and skip that turn.",
  "rulesCorneredTitle": "Accusation and Secret Finish",
  "rulesCornered": "An Active Innocent with both types of Evidence on the Cornered target may accuse, at most once per game. The attacker has the first 10-second slot, followed by Active players clockwise. A correct accusation wins alone; a wrong one eliminates both players. If nobody accuses, an Active Impostor may secretly finish a Cornered Innocent during a 10-second sealed window. If no finish occurs, the target may play Last Chance in the next 10-second window.",
  "rulesVictoryTitle": "Winning",
  "rulesVictory": "A correct accuser wins immediately. The Impostor wins when every Innocent is eliminated, even if the Impostor is Cornered. A Cornered Innocent still survives. If the Impostor permanently forfeits, the match is cancelled without a winner."
